  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configs (config_032: 0.7250, config_029: 0.7207, config_005: 0.7062) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, confirming these as strong choices. Transformer aggregation clearly outperforms avgpool (+0.019), and weighted vs concat fusion is nearly equivalent (0.004 gap). However, pca_n2000 as an RNA encoder has never been tested in any multimodal setup, leaving a key uncertainty: whether a simpler, cheaper linear projection can match the learned VAE (scvi_n200). This experiment (config_047: pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding all other components at their proven-best settings. If pca_n2000 is competitive, it offers a significantly cheaper alternative (PCA is a linear projection vs. a multi-step VAE training), reducing GPU cost. If it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 is essential and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer core. Expected relative cost: slightly lower than config_032 (3.60 GPU hrs), estimated ~2.5–3.5 GPU hours, since PCA encoding is far cheaper than scvi training while the ViT-L and transformer aggregation costs remain similar."
}

